    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Why daily use matters most
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        The strongest evidence for sunscreen and skin ageing comes from a randomised trial in Australia. It followed 903 adults younger than 55 for four and a half years. The people assigned to daily broad-spectrum sunscreen showed no detectable increase in skin ageing over that time, and their skin ageing was 24% less than in the group that used sunscreen only when they chose to.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23732711/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
    </p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        The lesson is practical. A sunscreen that feels pleasant enough to wear daily beats a better-sounding one that you skip.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        How to apply it properly
    </h2>

    <ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Apply before you go out.</strong> Sunscreen takes about 15 minutes to absorb and protect.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Use at least 1 teaspoon for your face,</strong> roughly the length of your index and middle fingers.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Consider two thin layers.</strong> In a laboratory study of 31 volunteers, a single application missed a median of 20% of the body surface, and a second consecutive application cut that to 9%.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29590142/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Reapply every two hours outdoors,</strong> and right after sweating or swimming.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Do not forget your neck and ears.</strong><a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a>
</li>
    </ol>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        The two-layer study was done on the whole body in swimwear, so treat its numbers as a guide and not a promise. It does show how easy it is to miss patches with a single quick pass.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:34px 0;padding:24px 26px;border-top:1px solid #B87330;border-bottom:1px solid #B87330;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 7px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;">Keep in mind</p>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            Your skin is exposed to UV rays whenever you go outside, including on cloudy days.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a> A sunscreen you apply every morning protects you on all of them.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Your morning order
    </h2>

    <ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Cleanse</strong> with a gentle cleanser.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Apply a serum if you use one.</strong> For <a href="/products/dark-spots-pore-control-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Dark Spots, Pore Control Serum</a>, that is 3 to 4 drops on damp skin.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;"><strong>Moisturise.</strong></li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Finish with sunscreen,</strong> as the last step before makeup.</li>
    </ol>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Dark Spots, Pore Control Serum is built for dark marks and uneven tone, and it works as the one active step in the routine. In the serum's own clinical study on 36 Indian women aged 24 to 44, with twice-daily use, 100% of patients improved dark spots in 8 weeks, and individual results may vary. The sunscreen that follows matters, because dermatologists say that effective care for dark marks begins with sunscreen.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a> Patch test the serum before first use.
    </p>

