    <h2 style="margin:56px 0 18px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Frequently asked questions
    </h2>

    <div style="border-top:2px solid #181818;">
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Is SPF 50 better than SPF 30 for the face?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Dermatologists recommend SPF 30 or higher, along with broad-spectrum coverage and water resistance.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a> Using enough and reapplying matters at least as much as the number.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How much sunscreen do I need for my face?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">At least 1 teaspoon, which is about the length of your index and middle fingers.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a> Applying it in two thin layers can reduce missed areas.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29590142/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Do I need sunscreen on cloudy days?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Yes. Your skin is exposed to the sun's UV rays every time you go outside, even on cloudy days.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Is tinted sunscreen worth it?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">It is worth it if you have dark marks or melasma. Dermatologists recommend tinted sunscreen with iron oxide for caring for dark spots, because iron oxide protects against visible light.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32335182/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How do I avoid a white cast?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Look for a formula that blends with your skin tone.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a> Tinted sunscreens come in many shades made for different skin tones.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32335182/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How often should I reapply?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Every two hours when you are outdoors, and straight after swimming or sweating.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/sun-protection/shade-clothing-sunscreen/how-to-apply-sunscreen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

